# Deliberate divergences. libSQL's Hrana transport releases a sqld namespace
# when its last connection closes, so the conformance tests must close every
# connection they open; leaving one open leaks the namespace for the whole run.
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/JSON1Test.java -- Hrana holds a namespace until its last connection closes, so the conformance copy closes the leaked per-test connections.
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/CachedRowSetTest.java -- Hrana holds a namespace until its last connection closes, so the conformance copy closes the leaked connection and asserts the row it reads.
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/InsertQueryTest.java -- upstream misuses the connection factory so the transaction is applied to a different connection and never asserts the result; the conformance copy reuses the transaction connection, asserts rollback and commit visibility, and asserts the final count (#51).
# divergence: src/test/java/org/sqlite/PreparedStatementThreadTest.java -- upstream swallows ExecutionException, which also wraps assertion failures; the conformance copy rethrows AssertionError so the race test can fail (#51).
